{"id":28,"date":"2022-11-21T12:25:09","date_gmt":"2022-11-21T12:25:09","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/?post_type=projects&#038;p=28"},"modified":"2025-04-16T00:36:54","modified_gmt":"2025-04-16T00:36:54","slug":"exford-primary-school","status":"publish","type":"projects","link":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/project\/exford-primary-school\/","title":{"rendered":"Exford Primary School"},"content":{"rendered":"\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-info\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__details\"\">\n\n                \n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Location<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Exford, Victoria<\/span><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Client name<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Victorian School Building Authority<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Value<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">$6.24 MIL<\/span><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Timeframe<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">2019-2022<\/span><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Contractor<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/orionbuilders.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Orion Builders<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Consultant team<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Structural &amp; Civil Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.adamseng.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Adams Consulting Engineers<\/a><br \/>\nServices Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.njmdesign.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NJM Design<\/a><br \/>\nAcoustic Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.renzotonin.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Renzo Tonin<\/a><br \/>\nLand Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.yellowpages.com.au\/vic\/hawthorn\/rickard-peter-associates-pty-ltd-14331807-listing.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Peter Rickard and Associates<\/a><br \/>\nLandscape Architect &#8211; Land Design Partnership &amp; Leftfield Design<br \/>\nAccess Consultant &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.disabilityaccessconsultants.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Equal Access<\/a><br \/>\nHydrogeologist &#8211; MSH Groundwater<br \/>\nBushfire Assessment &#8211; Keystone Alliance<br \/>\nGeotechnical Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.civiltest.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Civil Test<\/a><br \/>\nQuantity Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"https:\/\/mbmpl.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MBM<\/a><br \/>\nBuilding Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.duchateauchun.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">du Chateau Chun<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Photographer<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.yelp.com\/biz\/christopher-alexander-photography-blackburn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Christopher Alexander Photography<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                \n                \n                \n                                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__text\">\n                <p>The progressive rebirth of Exford Primary School from an overcrowded and under-resourced \u2018country\u2019 school on the suburban fringe to a fully resourced contemporary school is progressing over a number of stages following multiple rounds of significant state government funding.<\/p>\n<p>The school suffered from being comprised entirely of relocatable buildings and operated without mains water, sewer or stormwater connections and insufficient power and telecom services. Its relative isolation, surrounded by sheep paddocks, belied the suburban fringe that was approaching and driving significant growth in student numbers.<\/p>\n<p>Following extensive consultation with the broader school community and working closely with the VSBA, we developed a detailed master plan that allowed for the safe, functional and continuous operation of the school throughout planned multistage construction phases, as well as satisfying the School\u2019s rapidly expanding accommodation requirements.<\/p>\n<p>The completion of Stage 1 of the plan is a testament to the value placed in a considered design process in order to ensure a successful built outcome. At the core of this is that Architecture Matters listens, with recognition of the school\u2019s particular needs requiring a careful interpretation and application of VSBA\u2019s building quality guidelines.<\/p>\n<p>Early works to established adequate infrastructure services to the site provided a vital underpinning to the school\u2019s long-term viability.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n               <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"619\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-9.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Exford Primary School entrance gate\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-9.jpg 619w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-9-226x300.jpg 226w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 619px) 100vw, 619px\" \/>                           <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"620\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-9.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Exford Primary School front door\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-9.jpg 620w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-9-227x300.jpg 227w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"879\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-12.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Exford Primary School rainbow mural\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-12.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-12-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-12-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-12-768x511.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate block-quote\">\n        <div class=\"max-sm:w-full ml-auto w-1\/2\">\n            <div>\n                <blockquote>\n\n                <p>Exford Primary School demonstrates how facilitating the active participation of the school community in the design and development process can deliver buildings and spaces that will play a pivotal role in shaping the school\u2019s sense of place and identity for decades to come.<\/p>\n\n                \n                <\/blockquote>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-thirds-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div>\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/Sliding1.gif\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Exford Primary School blue carpeted classroom\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-text-image\">\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        <div class=\"grid mt-[30px] md:mt-[50px]\">\n\n            <div class=\"grid__text space-y-12\">\n                                <div><p>The Stage 1 works were successfully completed in July 2022, and included a new administration building incorporating staff amenities, a formal school entrance, a junior learning base building that accommodates eight general learning areas (GLAs), and student amenities. Extensive landscaping, coordination of infrastructure upgrades and integration with multiple existing relocatable buildings across the school site were also included.<\/p>\n<p>Once the Stage 1 works were underway and having proved the viability of the comprehensive redevelopment of the school whilst it remained in operation, substantial additional funding was granted to the school to enable the completion of the master plan as a three-stage project delivery to run over subsequent 18-months.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n                            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n                 <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"630\" height=\"744\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/B3A3570.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Exford Primary School front gate\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/B3A3570.jpg 630w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/B3A3570-254x300.jpg 254w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-thirds-image-right\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div>\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/Sliding2.gif\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Exford Primary School blue carpeted lobby\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"880\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-12.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-12.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-12-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-12-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-12-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-text-image\">\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        <div class=\"grid mt-[30px] md:mt-[50px]\">\n\n            <div class=\"grid__text space-y-12\">\n                                <div><p>Stage 2 commenced in December 2022, divided into three consecutive parts, A, B and C:<\/p>\n<p>Stage 2A is a two-level GLA and specialist building with student amenities and staff work areas.<\/p>\n<p>Stage 2B is a refurbishment of Building Education Revolution-era paired-5MOD relocatables that we have arranged symmetrically around a central gallery space to create a new library, science and food preparation facility.<\/p>\n<p>Stage 2C is a community hub building incorporating a full-sized gym with stage, physical education office, student amenities and canteen.<\/p>\n<p>Additionally, all remaining areas of the school will be progressively landscaped, with the sports field and playing surfaces being rebuilt or added.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n                            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n                             <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-carousel\">\n\n        <div class=\"swiper swiper-block\">\n\n            \n                <div class=\"swiper-wrapper\">\n                    \n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-69.png\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-69.png 962w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-69-300x200.png 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-69-768x512.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-44.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-